<title>USA: U.S. weekly soybean crush 25,938,000 bushels.</title>
<headline>U.S. weekly soybean crush 25,938,000 bushels.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-04-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>National Oilseed Processors Association weekly soybean crushings by reporting members (crushings/capacity in bu, soymeal exports in short tons):</p>
<p>			 04/09/97    04/02/97	Year-Ago</p>
<p> Crushings	 25,938,000  27,870,000    26,087,000</p>
<p> Meal Exports	 116,421     184,382	     N/A</p>
<p> Capacity-X	35,324,000  35,324,000    33,981,000</p>
<p> Capacity-Y	35,516,775  35,516,775	     N/A</p>
<p>X-Members reporting weekly. Y-Weekly reporters plus members reporting only monthly. N/A-Not Available. Totals may not agree due to rounding by NOPA. R-revised from 28,321,000  </p>
<p>NOPA reported the following soybean crushings and capacity use by state for the week, with comparisons, in bushels:</p>
<p>    CRUSHINGS --   04/09/97    04/02/97     Year-Ago</p>
<p> Illinois	   4,234,000   4,711,000     4,621,000</p>
<p> Ind, Ky, Ohio    4,826,000   4,950,000     4,323,000</p>
<p> Southeast	  3,846,000   4,355,000     4,133,000</p>
<p> South Central    2,388,000   2,777,000     2,795,000</p>
<p> Southwest	  3,824,000   4,043,000     3,255,000</p>
<p> Iowa		 5,051,000   5,071,000     5,041,000</p>
<p> Minn,ND,SD,Mont  1,768,000   1,964,000     1,919,000</p>
<p> Total U.S.	25,938,000  27,870,000    26,087,000</p>
